From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:20:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fdcan: Count only bus-off entry transitions

M_CAN sets IR.BO whenever PSR.BO changes, including when bus-off recovery
completes.  Incrementing the diagnostic counter for every BO interrupt
therefore reports two episodes for each recovered fault.

Read PSR and count bus-off only when its BO state is set.  Handle BO and
protocol-error interrupts together so the state check does not consume
LEC before error accounting reads it.  Clearing INIT on entry still
starts the controller's normal ISO CAN recovery sequence.

Apply the same handling to STM32, ATSAM, and ATSAMD.  Native register
harnesses cover entry, recovery, repeated faults, counter rollover, and
simultaneous protocol errors, and reproduce the double count in the
previous implementation.  Firmware builds pass for STM32H723, G0B1,
G474, SAME70, SAME51, and SAMC21.  No wire format changes are made.

Signed-off-by: JR Lomas <lomas.jr@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8b540a8e3a98faaf3fea7ff0c741eea9b79dfcdb)

diff --git a/src/atsam/fdcan.c b/src/atsam/fdcan.c
index d5370dd4..2282eacd 100644
--- a/src/atsam/fdcan.c
+++ b/src/atsam/fdcan.c
@@ -294,25 +294,16 @@ CAN_IRQHandler(void)
             canbus_notify_tx();
         }
     }
-    if (ir & MCAN_IR_BO) {
-        /*
-         * The M_CAN core enters software-initialization mode by setting INIT
-         * when its transmit error counter reaches bus-off.  In that mode it is
-         * completely disconnected from the bus and will remain so even after
-         * the wiring fault disappears; there is no automatic bus-off-management
-         * option.  Clear INIT after acknowledging the event to start the ISO
-         * CAN recovery sequence.  The controller still waits for the required
-         * 129 occurrences of 11 recessive bits, so this does not bypass or
-         * shorten the protocol's recovery safety interval.
-         */
-        CANx->MCAN_IR = MCAN_IR_BO;
-        CAN_Errors.bus_off++;
-        CANx->MCAN_CCCR &= ~MCAN_CCCR_INIT;
-    }
-    if (ir & (MCAN_IR_PED | MCAN_IR_PEA)) {
-        // Bus error
+    if (ir & (MCAN_IR_BO | MCAN_IR_PED | MCAN_IR_PEA)) {
+        // PSR reads clear LEC; share one snapshot for state and error handling.
         uint32_t psr = CANx->MCAN_PSR;
-        CANx->MCAN_IR = MCAN_IR_PED | MCAN_IR_PEA;
+        CANx->MCAN_IR = ir & (MCAN_IR_BO | MCAN_IR_PED | MCAN_IR_PEA);
+        if ((ir & MCAN_IR_BO) && (psr & MCAN_PSR_BO)) {
+            // BO interrupts on entry and recovery.  Count only entry, and
+            // clear INIT to start the controller's ISO CAN recovery sequence.
+            CAN_Errors.bus_off++;
+            CANx->MCAN_CCCR &= ~MCAN_CCCR_INIT;
+        }
         uint32_t lec = psr & MCAN_PSR_LEC_Msk;
         if (lec && lec != 7) {
             if (lec >= 3 && lec <= 5)
